The portable C in the scenario setup-clock: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/setup-clock.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 1, 5, 7, 14 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the Configuration of the setup has no Execute options, which were Memory
allocation, Quick execute commands and TSR manager: the Keyboard options stand
five rows further up, at the top of the right half, with the last five rows of
the right half empty; and Screen and Mouse of the setup has no Screen output:
the Other options and the Mouse options stand five rows further up, where that
group was, with the right half empty below them. The mouse pointer exchanges
the colours of the cell that it is on, the middle of the screen where nothing
has moved it: the lines have moved under it, and it stays

